WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.408
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.708 --> 00:00:09.269
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:16.076
Unit eleven: Causative (have something done). Today you will say that someone else does a service for you.

4
00:00:16.376 --> 00:00:18.970
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.933 --> 00:00:22.934
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:25.017
Have something done.

7
00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:29.340
Have something done means to arrange for another person to do a job.

8
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.601
I had my hair cut.

9
00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:35.020
Your turn. Say: Have something done.

10
00:00:37.867 --> 00:00:39.262
Have something done.

11
00:00:40.017 --> 00:00:41.285
Get something done.

12
00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:45.490
Get something done means an informal way to arrange a service.

13
00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:47.769
I got my phone fixed.

14
00:00:48.383 --> 00:00:50.827
Your turn. Say: Get something done.

15
00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:54.946
Get something done.

16
00:00:55.683 --> 00:00:56.847
Service.

17
00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.349
Service means work that someone does for you.

18
00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:02.474
The service was fast.

19
00:01:03.083 --> 00:01:05.631
Your turn. Say: Service.

20
00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:09.433
Service.

21
00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:11.382
Someone else.

22
00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:14.812
Someone else means a person other than you.

23
00:01:15.417 --> 00:01:17.068
Someone else cleaned it.

24
00:01:17.683 --> 00:01:20.997
Your turn. Say: Someone else.

25
00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:25.125
Someone else.

26
00:01:25.883 --> 00:01:27.233
Passive causative.

27
00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:32.596
Passive causative means the structure have + object + past participle.

28
00:01:33.183 --> 00:01:35.729
A passive causative shows a service.

29
00:01:36.317 --> 00:01:39.259
Your turn. Say: Passive causative.

30
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.577
Passive causative.

31
00:01:44.317 --> 00:01:45.120
Haircut.

32
00:01:46.117 --> 00:01:48.778
Haircut means the act of having your hair cut.

33
00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:50.605
I got a haircut.

34
00:01:51.217 --> 00:01:54.206
Your turn. Say: Haircut.

35
00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:57.940
Haircut.

36
00:01:58.683 --> 00:01:59.673
Repair.

37
00:02:00.683 --> 00:02:02.880
Repair means to fix something broken.

38
00:02:03.483 --> 00:02:04.786
They repair bikes.

39
00:02:05.383 --> 00:02:08.396
Your turn. Say: Repair.

40
00:02:11.233 --> 00:02:12.374
Repair.

41
00:02:13.117 --> 00:02:13.990
Arrange.

42
00:02:14.983 --> 00:02:17.087
Arrange means to organise something.

43
00:02:17.683 --> 00:02:19.195
I arranged the delivery.

44
00:02:19.783 --> 00:02:22.099
Your turn. Say: Arrange.

45
00:02:24.933 --> 00:02:25.969
Arrange.

46
00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:30.429
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:33.480
Visal, did you cut your hair yourself?

48
00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:46.390
No, I had it cut. Have something done means someone else does the service for me. I did not do it myself. The structure is have + object + past participle.

49
00:02:47.483 --> 00:02:48.670
How do we form it?

50
00:02:49.783 --> 00:03:04.713
Subject + have + object + past participle: I had my phone repaired. She is having her house painted. They will have the car washed. In informal speech, get can replace have: I got my phone fixed.

51
00:03:05.817 --> 00:03:07.259
Why is it useful?

52
00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:18.818
It shows that a service is done by someone else, without naming the person. Do not say I repaired my phone if a technician did it. Say I had my phone repaired.

53
00:03:19.967 --> 00:03:21.780
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:22.617 --> 00:03:27.437
Grammar focus: Causative: have and get plus object plus past participle.

55
00:03:27.737 --> 00:03:29.017
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:29.717 --> 00:03:31.600
I had my hair cut yesterday.

57
00:03:32.517 --> 00:03:34.377
She is having her house painted.

58
00:03:35.283 --> 00:03:36.842
We got the car washed.

59
00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:44.678
Have / get + object + past participle shows that someone else does a service for you. It is not the same as doing it yourself.

60
00:03:45.417 --> 00:03:49.137
Be careful! Don't say: I repaired my car at a garage.

61
00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:54.168
Say: I had my car repaired at a garage.

62
00:03:54.468 --> 00:03:57.849
Use have + object + past participle.

63
00:03:58.633 --> 00:04:01.112
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:03.157
Having Things Done.

65
00:04:03.457 --> 00:04:05.398
I had my hair cut yesterday.

66
00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.841
My phone broke, so I had it repaired.

67
00:04:09.833 --> 00:04:11.914
My parents are having the house painted.

68
00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.958
We got our car washed this morning.

69
00:04:15.967 --> 00:04:18.976
A service is work that another person does for us.

70
00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:23.964
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:24.817 --> 00:04:27.072
I blank my phone repaired last week.

72
00:04:27.372 --> 00:04:30.700
A, had. B, repaired. C, did.

73
00:04:34.233 --> 00:04:36.094
The answer is A: had.

74
00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.006
She is having her hair blank.

75
00:04:39.306 --> 00:04:42.599
A, cut. B, cutting. C, cuts.

76
00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:47.843
The answer is A: cut.

77
00:04:48.983 --> 00:04:51.331
Which sentence means someone else did it?

78
00:04:51.631 --> 00:04:56.910
A, I cut my hair.. B, I had my hair cut.. C, I am cutting my hair..

79
00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:03.244
The answer is B: I had my hair cut..

80
00:05:04.383 --> 00:05:06.069
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:06.369 --> 00:05:13.134
A, I have repaired my car by a mechanic.. B, I had my car repaired.. C, I had repaired my car..

82
00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:19.141
The answer is B: I had my car repaired..

83
00:05:20.283 --> 00:05:22.829
According to the reading, what is a service?

84
00:05:23.129 --> 00:05:28.523
A, work done for us by another person. B, a type of food. C, a school.

85
00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:35.308
The answer is A: work done for us by another person.

86
00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.489
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:43.058
Write a sentence about a service you have had done recently.

88
00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.362
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:53.662 --> 00:06:05.570
I had my bicycle repaired last week. The mechanic changed the tyre and cleaned the chain. I use had + object + past participle because someone else did the work for me.

90
00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:07.788
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:08.683 --> 00:06:15.585
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and causative: have and get plus object plus past participle.

92
00:06:15.885 --> 00:06:20.743
Today's value is practical wisdom. Judge ideas by how well they work in real life.

93
00:06:21.043 --> 00:06:23.289
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

94
00:06:23.589 --> 00:06:26.706
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

